      "content": "that's a helpful distinction. so for kenji/japan, you're saying premium is muted and minimalist, but for amara/nigeria, it's more about warmth and bold colors. \n\ni'm worried though—if we go too \"bold\" or \"vibrant\" for the nigerian market, does that risk making the app look less \"professional\" or \"serious\" compared to the minimalist version we'd give to a japanese user? like, is there a reason why \"premium\" for one group requires restraint while the other requires more visual stimulation? i'm trying to understand if we're accidentally pigeonholing certain users into a more \"expressive\" category vs a more \"sophisticated\" one.",
